//! What the toolchain's natives read of the machine a program runs on, as an effect: a function
//! whose row names `native.read` asks the machine through one, so nothing takes its answer for a
//! function of its arguments. No operation is performed and nothing handles one: an effect's real
//! handler (`host for`) names it beside the effect it discharges, and the roots that run under the
//! handler never see it.

/// Asking the machine through a native.
pub nondet effect native {}
